# Cloudflare Pages / Netlify SPA fallback.
#
# React Router owns every path client-side, but the edge only has the files
# in dist/. Without this rule a direct hit on /map, /volunteer or a shared
# alert link returns the host's 404 page instead of the app — which is the
# case that matters most here, since those links get forwarded around during
# an incident by people who never touched the home page.
#
# 200 (rewrite), not 302 (redirect): the URL in the address bar must survive
# so the router can read it on boot.
/*  /index.html  200
